 "result": "This repo is Flask renamed to `tessel`, and the names differ from Flask's.\n\n**How they get in**\n- `_base_template_vars()` in `src/tessel/templating.py:21` returns `{\"g\": ctx.g}`, plus `request` when `ctx.has_request`. `session` is not copied in, because the `session` proxy has to stay a proxy so access is tracked (comment at line 30).\n- `Scaffold.__init__` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:184` seeds `template_ctx_injectors` with `{None: [_base_template_vars]}`.\n- `App.fill_template_scope()` in `src/tessel/app.py:588` runs those injector functions. It runs the app-wide ones (`None`) first, then the request's bundle ones, and merges the results into the context. Values passed directly to `render_template` are re-applied last, so they win.\n- `render_template` and `render_template_string` call `fill_template_scope` at `templating.py:125` and `:167`.\n\n**Adding your own**\n- Decorate a function with `@app.ctx_injector` (`Scaffold.ctx_injector`, `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`). It should return a dict whose keys become template variables.\n- On a bundle, `@bundle.ctx_injector` applies only to that bundle's views. `@bundle.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:644`) applies to every template.\n- For static values or functions, `app.jinja_env.globals[...]` is the alternative, as in `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:825`.\n\nI didn't find `session` or `config` injected anywhere in `src`. The docstring at `app.py:592` claims `request`, `session`, `config` and `g` are injected, but the code only does `g` and `request`.",
